# Keep shell scripts and plain-text data files LF on every platform, so Windows
# CI (default core.autocrlf=true) doesn't check them out as CRLF and break tools
# that parse them line-by-line — e.g. capi/scripts/check_header_sync.sh reading
# capi/scripts/header_sync_allow.txt.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# crates/ingestion/tests/fixtures/pdf/sample.pdf is deliberately uncompressed,
# so it is pure ASCII and git's auto-detection classifies it as *text*. A
# Windows checkout would then rewrite its line endings, which shifts every byte
# after the first newline and silently invalidates the offsets in the PDF
# `xref` table. `-text` (rather than `binary`) disables that conversion while
# keeping the file diffable, which is the whole reason it is uncompressed.
*.pdf -text
